        "srcSet": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/6/c/6c1bbfe26254d930f26e0bef59501c24b963bf74_2_690x302.png, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/6/c/6c1bbfe26254d930f26e0bef59501c24b963bf74_2_1035x453.png 1.5x, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/6/c/6c1bbfe26254d930f26e0bef59501c24b963bf74_2_1380x604.png 2x",
        "alt": "Screenshot_Import_Form_Execution",
        "width": "690",
        "height": "302"
       }
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "a": {
      "start": "3"
     },
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "Back Up And Remove All:"
           ]
          },
          " A highly useful feature for maintenance windows. This action reads current schedules, securely backs them up directly into the Source object’s ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "connectorAttributes"
           ]
          },
          ", and then deletes the active schedules, effectively “pausing” all aggregations tenant-wide."
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "How the backup works:"
           ]
          },
          " The script executes a ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "PATCH"
           ]
          },
          " request to the ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "/sources/v1/:id"
           ]
          },
          " endpoint (using the ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "application/json-patch+json"
           ]
          },
          " content type) to inject custom keys directly into the source’s configuration. Specifically, it saves the current CRON strings into two new variables: ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "BackUpAccountAggregationCRON"
           ]
          },
          " and ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "BackUpGroupAggregationCRON"
           ]
          },
          ". By utilizing ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "connectorAttributes"
           ]
          },
          ", the data stays safely attached to the source itself within SailPoint, preventing the need to manage external backup files during a maintenance window."
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "div",
     "a": {
      "class": "d-wrap",
      "data-wrap": "center"
     },
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "lightbox",
       "a": {
        "full": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/original/3X/d/a/dab502f69d774177f8ef779d368e4d73e0da45ed.png",
        "src": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/d/a/dab502f69d774177f8ef779d368e4d73e0da45ed_2_690x295.png",
        "srcSet": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/d/a/dab502f69d774177f8ef779d368e4d73e0da45ed_2_690x295.png, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/d/a/dab502f69d774177f8ef779d368e4d73e0da45ed_2_1035x442.png 1.5x, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/d/a/dab502f69d774177f8ef779d368e4d73e0da45ed_2_1380x590.png 2x",
        "alt": "Screenshot_BackUpAndRemoveAll_Form_Execution",
        "width": "690",
        "height": "295"
       }
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "a": {
      "start": "4"
     },
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "Restore All:"
           ]
          },
          " Reads the backed-up CRON strings from the Source objects and re-activates all schedules, returning the tenant to normal operation."
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "How the restore works:"
           ]
          },
          " The script queries all sources and checks their ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "connectorAttributes"
           ]
          },
          " specifically for the ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "BackUpAccountAggregationCRON"
           ]
          },
          " and ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "BackUpGroupAggregationCRON"
           ]
          },
          " variables. If a source does not have these variables (meaning it had no active schedule when the backup was taken), the script safely skips it and moves to the next source. If it does find the backup variables, it issues a ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "POST"
           ]
          },
          " request to recreate the schedule, followed by a final ",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "PATCH"
           ]
          },
          " request (",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "op: \"remove\""
           ]
          },
          ") to clean up the backup variables from the source configuration so no stale data is left behind."
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
