    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "architectural-decision-why-pag-powershell-vs-native-workflows"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Architectural Decision: Why PAG & PowerShell vs. Native Workflows?"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      "A common question when designing workflow automations in SailPoint is whether to rely strictly on native workflow actions or extend capabilities using the Privileged Action Gateway (PAG):"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Why PAG + PowerShell for this solution:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "High-Throughput Parallel Processing:"
             ]
            },
            " Large enterprise tenants often manage 100+ sources. Iterating through hundreds of sources sequentially via native Workflow HTTP Request loops is constrained by execution timeouts and API pagination overhead. PowerShell Runspace pools allow multi-threaded concurrency (10–15 parallel threads), reducing execution from 20+ minutes down to seconds."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Dynamic File System & Dropdown Population:"
             ]
            },
            " Native workflow forms cannot dynamically read local directories. The helper script (",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "Get-AggregationScheduleFiles.ps1"
             ]
            },
            ") reads the export directory on disk and injects the filenames into the interactive form dropdown in real time."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Local File Archiving & Transport:"
             ]
            },
            " Exporting schedules directly into timestamped CSV artifacts on the PAG server and automatically dispatching them via SMTP provides an off-platform backup trail that survives tenant configuration changes."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "When a Native Workflow-Only Approach Suffices:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "If your tenant has a small footprint (e.g., fewer than 10–15 sources) or if you only need to pause/resume specific, targeted sources, you can build a 100% native Workflow. Using the native ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "HTTP Request"
             ]
            },
            " action against ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "/sources/v1/:id/schedules"
             ]
            },
            " inside a simple loop avoids the requirement for an on-premises PAG server or local Windows host."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "prerequisites"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Prerequisites"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      "To successfully implement this solution, your environment will need the following in place:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Privileged Action Gateway (PAG):"
         ]
        },
        " A configured PAG instance to bridge SailPoint Workflows with your local scripts."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Local Windows Server:"
         ]
        },
        " A server to host the PowerShell scripts and provide a directory (e.g., ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "C:\\Scripts\\Aggregation Exports"
         ]
        },
        ") to write and read the CSV backup files."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "SMTP Setup:"
         ]
        },
        " Valid SMTP credentials and server details for the main script to dispatch the exported ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          ".csv"
         ]
        },
        " files to your email."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "API Credentials:"
         ]
        },
        " A SailPoint Personal Access Token (Client ID & Secret) with the appropriate scopes (",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "idn:sources:manage"
         ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "idn:sources:read"
         ]
        },
        ") for the script to execute the API calls."
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "safe-use-testing-backup-validation"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Safe Use, Testing & Backup Validation"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      "Because actions like ",
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Back Up And Remove All"
       ]
      },
      " and bulk ",
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Import"
       ]
      },
      " operate tenant-wide, operational discipline and safety controls are essential before running them in production:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Pre-Flight Testing in Sandbox:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "Always deploy and validate the Form, Workflow, and PowerShell scripts in your sandbox or staging tenant first."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "Run the ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Export"
             ]
            },
            " action and verify that the generated CSV contains the expected source IDs, names, and non-null CRON expressions."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Backup Validation Before Deletion:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "When using ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Export"
             ]
            },
            ", inspect the generated CSV file in ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "C:\\Scripts\\Aggregation Exports"
             ]
            },
            " (or your received email) to ensure the row count matches your total scheduled sources."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "When using ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Back Up And Remove All"
             ]
            },
            ", spot-check 2–3 active sources via the SailPoint Admin UI or the ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "/sources/v1/:id"
             ]
            },
            " API to verify that ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "BackUpAccountAggregationCRON"
             ]
            },
            " and/or ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "BackUpGroupAggregationCRON"
             ]
            },
            " have been successfully written to ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "connectorAttributes"
             ]
            },
            " ",
            {
             "t": "em",
             "c": [
              "before"
             ]
            },
            " assuming the backup succeeded."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Safety Confirmations in the Form:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            "The Workflow Form includes required confirmation toggles for destructive actions. Administrators must explicitly acknowledge and toggle the confirmation checkbox before the workflow triggers a tenant-wide pause or overwrite."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Post-Execution Verification:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "After Pausing:"
             ]
            },
            " Navigate to a source in the ISC Admin UI and check the schedule is turned off."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "After Restoring:"
             ]
            },
            " Run a fresh ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Export"
             ]
            },
            " action and compare the new CSV against your original baseline backup using a diff tool to confirm 100% parity."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "user-interface"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "User Interface"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "Input Fields:"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Options:"
             ]
            },
            " Export, Import, Back Up And Remove All, Restore All."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Import Options:"
             ]
            },
            " A dynamic dropdown populated with the available CSV files on the server (using a helper PowerShell script)."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Warnings:"
             ]
            },
            " Toggle confirmations for the tenant-wide Pause/Restore actions."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "User Experience:"
           ]
          },
          " By using a dynamic workflow form, we ensure admins don’t need to manually type file paths or rely on hardcoded variables. The helper script (",
          {
           "t": "code",
           "c": [
            "Get-AggregationScheduleFiles.ps1"
           ]
          },
          ") fetches the available export files directly from the server for easy selection."
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Form Definition Code:"
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "br"
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "a",
       "a": {
        "class": "attachment",
        "href": "https://developer.sailpoint.com/discuss/uploads/short-url/yybLPjXFGMg7LIbw9oN4abFMopW.json"
       },
       "c": [
        "Form-AggregationScheduleManager.json"
       ]
      },
      " (7.2 KB)"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "back-end-workflow"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Back End Workflow"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "div",
     "a": {
      "class": "d-wrap",
      "data-wrap": "center"
     },
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "lightbox",
       "a": {
        "full": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/original/3X/c/6/c6f433d94f0cb8ff20a480b6761027db5256f690.png",
        "src": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/c/6/c6f433d94f0cb8ff20a480b6761027db5256f690_2_383x500.png",
        "srcSet": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/c/6/c6f433d94f0cb8ff20a480b6761027db5256f690_2_383x500.png, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/c/6/c6f433d94f0cb8ff20a480b6761027db5256f690_2_574x750.png 1.5x, https://global.discourse-cdn.com/sailpoint/optimized/3X/c/6/c6f433d94f0cb8ff20a480b6761027db5256f690_2_766x1000.png 2x",
        "alt": "AggregationScheduleManager20260809",
        "width": "383",
        "height": "500"
       }
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Trigger:"
         ]
        },
        " This solution utilizes an ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "Interactive Trigger"
         ]
        },
        " so we can launch it directly from the Launchers UI."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Helper Script via PAG:"
         ]
        },
        " The first step runs the ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "Get-AggregationScheduleFiles.ps1"
         ]
        },
        " script to load the available CSVs from the server and populate the interactive form dropdown."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Interactive Form:"
         ]
        },
        " The user is presented with the dynamic form to select their desired action."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Main Script Execution:"
         ]
        },
        " Based on the form selection, the workflow passes the arguments to the ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "Manage-AggregationSchedules.ps1"
         ]
        },
        " script which does the heavy lifting via APIs."
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Workflow Code:"
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "br"
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "a",
       "a": {
        "class": "attachment",
        "href": "https://developer.sailpoint.com/discuss/uploads/short-url/8QxiawwsAaHWMVkBPWeYMletG4x.json"
       },
       "c": [
        "Workflow-AggregationScheduleManager.json"
       ]
      },
      " (9.3 KB)"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "powershell-execution-api-highlights"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "PowerShell Execution & API Highlights"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "High Performance (Parallel Processing):"
         ]
        },
        " Iterating through hundreds of sources sequentially via REST APIs is incredibly slow. The main script (",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "Manage-AggregationSchedules.ps1"
         ]
        },
        ") utilizes PowerShell Runspace Pools (multi-threading) to process 10-15 sources concurrently, drastically reducing execution time from minutes to seconds."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "API Adherence:"
         ]
        },
        " The scripts adhere to SailPoint’s newest API structures, specifically utilizing the ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "sources/v1"
         ]
        },
        " endpoint for patching source attributes, and the ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "sources/v1/:id/schedules"
         ]
        },
        " endpoint."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Complete Audit Trail:"
         ]
        },
        " Implements a comprehensive, timestamped logging framework. Every action, parameter, and API exception is logged to a ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "logs.txt"
         ]
        },
        " file in the script directory, providing perfect visibility for troubleshooting PAG executions."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Error Handling, Rate Limiting & Mid-Flight Recovery:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "API Resilience & Throttling:"
             ]
            },
            " All API requests incorporate error trapping for HTTP 429 (Rate Limit Exceeded) and transient network timeouts. If a rate limit is encountered, the script backs off exponentially before retrying."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Per-Source Graceful Degradation:"
             ]
            },
            " The script encapsulates each source update in individual ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "try...catch"
             ]
            },
            " blocks. If one source encounters an issue (e.g., locked source or invalid CRON syntax), the failure is logged as a ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "[WARN]"
             ]
            },
            " to ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "logs.txt"
             ]
            },
            ", and the runspace continues processing all remaining sources rather than crashing midway."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Partial Failure Recovery:"
             ]
            },
            " In the event of a partial run, the administrator can inspect ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "logs.txt"
             ]
            },
            " to identify the skipped source IDs. Because the backup data is stored directly in ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "connectorAttributes"
             ]
            },
            ", running ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Restore All"
             ]
            },
            " again is idempotent, it will safely re-process any source that still has the backup attributes present."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Fatal Failures:"
             ]
            },
            " A custom ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "Throw-Error"
             ]
            },
            " function catches fundamental system faults (e.g., failed OAuth authentication, unreadable CSV file, or unavailable network gateway) to immediately halt the script and return an explicit error code to the SailPoint Workflow engine."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "PowerShell Scripts:"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "Helper Script:"
           ]
          },
          "  ",
          {
           "t": "a",
           "a": {
            "class": "attachment",
            "href": "https://developer.sailpoint.com/discuss/uploads/short-url/gDp099njYu51jG0X6Gvc6GO1Jy8.ps1"
           },
           "c": [
            "Get-AggregationScheduleFiles.ps1"
           ]
          },
          " (1.5 KB)"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "p",
         "c": [
          {
           "t": "strong",
           "c": [
            "Main Script:"
           ]
          },
          " ",
          {
           "t": "a",
           "a": {
            "class": "attachment",
            "href": "https://developer.sailpoint.com/discuss/uploads/short-url/AqwlXjcIqsplb0siKoHS1pTN7cO.ps1"
           },
           "c": [
            "Manage-AggregationSchedules.ps1"
           ]
          },
          " (12.4 KB)"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "a": {
      "id": "considerations-best-practices"
     },
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Considerations & Best Practices"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "c": [
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "PAG Compatibility:"
         ]
        },
        " The scripts are written to ensure compatibility with Windows Server PowerShell 5.1 (using ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "-UseBasicParsing"
         ]
        },
        " for ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "Invoke-RestMethod"
         ]
        },
        ") and enforce TLS 1.2 for secure API authentication."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Permissioning:"
         ]
        },
        " The launcher should only be granted to admins, as this provides the ability to enable/disable aggregations completely across the tenant."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Token Security:"
         ]
        },
        " The main script uses standard OAuth Client Credentials. Ensure the client ID and secret have the necessary ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "idn:sources:manage"
         ]
        },
        " and ",
        {
         "t": "code",
         "c": [
          "idn:sources:read"
         ]
        },
        " scopes."
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Credential & Secret Protection:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Never Hardcode Secrets:"
             ]
            },
            " While the example script displays placeholder variables (",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "YOUR_CLIENT_ID"
             ]
            },
            ", ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET"
             ]
            },
            "), production deployments should ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "never"
             ]
            },
            " store plaintext API secrets in ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              ".ps1"
             ]
            },
            " files."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Recommended Storage:"
             ]
            },
            " Store your Client ID and Secret in ",
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Windows Credential Manager"
             ]
            },
            ", read them from system environment variables, retrieve them via Azure Key Vault / HashiCorp Vault, or pass them as secure workflow inputs through the PAG."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Least Privilege:"
             ]
            },
            " Ensure the API Personal Access Token or OAuth Client uses only the minimum scopes required: ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "idn:sources:read"
             ]
            },
            " and ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "idn:sources:manage"
             ]
            },
            "."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
       "t": "li",
       "c": [
        {
         "t": "strong",
         "c": [
          "Log Sanitization & Access Control:"
         ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
         "t": "ul",
         "c": [
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Token Masking:"
             ]
            },
            " Bearer tokens and HTTP Authorization headers are stripped and excluded from all ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "Write-Log"
             ]
            },
            " operations to prevent sensitive credentials from ever landing in ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "logs.txt"
             ]
            },
            "."
           ]
          },
          "\n",
          {
           "t": "li",
           "c": [
            {
             "t": "strong",
             "c": [
              "Directory Permissions (ACLs):"
             ]
            },
            " Restrict NTFS file permissions on ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "C:\\Scripts\\Aggregation Exports"
             ]
            },
            " and ",
            {
             "t": "code",
             "c": [
              "logs.txt"
             ]
            },
            ". Only the PAG service account and authorized server administrators should have read/write access to these paths."
           ]
          },
          "\n"
         ]
        },
        "\n"
       ]
      },
      "\n",
